{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1316770-ever-ran-a-game-using-danse-macabre-content","id":1316770,"title":"Ever ran a game using Danse Macabre content?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-06-05T22:51:57-07:00","id":1316770,"title":"Ever ran a game using Danse Macabre content?","content":"This book came up in a recent conversation and I remembered how much I loved the tier 1 take on Clans, the tier 3 Conspiracies, and the Atrocity Dice mechanic. It\u2019s a pretty stellar toolkit, and in the running for my favorite 1e book; has anyone else ever gotten any part of it to the table?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T03:50:15-07:00","id":1316793,"title":"","content":"Yes. Yes! YES! <br /> I used a lot of that book. <br /> Social combat is an instant standout, in particular the inclusion of the Edge. (Winning at social combat grants you bonuses to stuff like hunting and combat)<br /> I also used the covenants at different tiers to represent different goals and iterations of the covenants. I never read the covenant specific books but danse macabre filled that gap perfectly for me.<br /> I might flick through it this evening and reminisce. <br /> For me one of the strongest books that melded mechanics, narrative and setting perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1161,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","user":"Gravitas Man","date":". 06-06-2019, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T07:17:19-07:00","id":1316818,"title":"","content":"I'm using Harbingers in my current campaign. One of the players is part of the covenant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T07:29:38-07:00","id":1316821,"title":"","content":"I took the teir 1 carthian movement for one of the political factions in my city, and might use the teir 3 as well, depending on how things go.<br /> <br /> I love the Atrocity dice system and really want to integrate it. I've been trying to work on a Gangrel merit that works similarly. <br /> <br /> I used the Anchor schema because one of my players didn't have time to really invest in character creation/session 0. This was really useful because we started playing immediately after embrace, and I've been trying to foreground mortal relationships. <br /> <br /> I'd definitely like to try out the Hell is Other People system.<br /> <br /> I appreciated the advice for Devotion creation. Haven't had a chance to use any of the quest stuff, but I if the opportunity arises, I plan to.<br /> <br /> I also wrote up a Chronicle Pitch, (loosely) using the Danse Macabre format.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T08:14:03-07:00","id":1316830,"title":"","content":"Atrocity is a favorite of mine. It works great in <i>Vampire</i>, and I also adapted it for the dark side in a <i>Star Wars</i> game.<br /> <br /> I'm currently playing with a revision that uses both atrocity and a version of Humanity we didn't have time to finish for VtR2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T09:05:20-07:00","id":1316844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1316770-ever-ran-a-game-using-danse-macabre-content?p=1316830#post1316830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Atrocity is a favorite of mine. It works great in <i>Vampire</i>, and I also adapted it for the dark side in a <i>Star Wars</i> game.<br /> <br /> I'm currently playing with a revision that uses both atrocity and a version of Humanity we didn't have time to finish for VtR2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that sounds exciting! Will it end up on Patreon and/or the STVault when it's done?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T10:15:20-07:00","id":1316857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1316770-ever-ran-a-game-using-danse-macabre-content?p=1316844#post1316844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now that sounds exciting! Will it end up on Patreon and/or the STVault when it's done?</div> </div> </div> </div>If people are interested, I could do an STV version!<br /> <br /> I'm taking some ideas from <i>The Danse Macabre</i> and some non-vampire crime stuff I've run and developing them a little further, so:<br /> <br /> For a start: Humanity means roughly what it does now, but it merges with Willpower. So Humanity fluctuates, and it's also something you <i>earn</i>, by interacting with your Touchstones and hitting upward breaking points and so on.<br /> <br /> (Being more human isn't saccharine niceness or anything, but if you can crack a smile and save an orphanage, that's usually not going to <i>lose</i> you Humanity.)<br /> <br /> Masquerade and Requiem come back (and I call them Mask and Dirge, for convenience), and act a lot like Origin and Role in <i>Bleeding Edge</i>. The twist is that Mask starts high but is rough to hold onto, while Dirge starts low, but is a cheap buy.<br /> <br /> Disciplines... well, they're getting a look, too, but I need to dice-test my ideas some more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T00:40:38-07:00","id":1317754,"title":"","content":"I recently ran a game that focused on the Commonwealth, the tier three Conspiracy. <br /> <br /> The player characters awoke, with their minds all foggy and confused, in a hidden Commonwealth city were kindred and mortals live out in the open, side by side. It was an exploration about gaslighting on a large scale, where the players characters didn't know if the city was the norm or their foggy memories of living hidden among mortals was something that really happened. <br /> <br /> Somewhat inspired by that M Night Shyamalan film, The Village.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Organizer for the Dead Gamers Society: The So Cal World of Darkness Meetup. </span><a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/85-drumheller","name":"Drumheller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar85_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T06:32:41-07:00","id":1317787,"title":"","content":"That sounds really cool. How'd it go?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T07:41:43-07:00","id":1326463,"title":"","content":"Must admit i have only most foggy recollections of the book, the group i did play with for a time was somewhat haphazard in looking for &amp; adopting stuff from books beyond the core, mostly from bloodline, covenant &amp; clanbooks, if memory tricks me not.<br /> <br /> That and some bits from other games i would use to &quot;upgrade&quot; some of the bits &amp; concepts from Mythologies and some other places:<br /> <br /> - <b><i>Awakening</i></b>'s Oneiros &amp; astral travel mechanics i would use to expand concepts from the &quot;Understanding the Fog of Eternity&quot; chapter. This would indirectly connect with the Alucinor and Usiri bloodlines, the Dream Visions merit from the Mekhet clanbook, dream-drinking from &quot;Sleep of Reason&quot; chapter - and the Sightless Mother.<br /> <br /> - <i><b>Book of Dead</b></i> for &quot;the Second Death&quot; realm. This would work as a deeper layer in the &quot;astral torpor travels&quot; of kindred, going into the Underworld (or at least a specific realm within it). Shenanigans were had with dead kindred stealing the bodies of torpid &quot;deep divers&quot;, psychocomps/&quot;reapers&quot; entering our world after them (or diablerists with their patchwork souls) under certain (un)auspicious circunstances, a tie-in of sorts with the &quot;Blood Curses&quot; chapter, and the occasional Mnemovore spawned when one such capture was &quot;botched&quot; somehow.<br /> <br /> - <b><i>Intruders: Encounters with the Abyss</i></b> would give me abyssal spiders infections with their mind control-inducing powers, that would mesh with the bees, powers &amp; manias of the Melissidae bloodline.<br /> <br /> - <i><b>Skinchangers</b></i>, from there i took the undead-wrangling Kanaima vengeance spirits, that served as expies/foils to the Strix in our games - and &quot;sire&quot; of one of the PCs.<br /> <br /> - Forsaken's <b><i>Predators </i></b>i stole some monsters from to become the &quot;Nonatii&quot;, the Neverborn, ur-vampire beasts born from the blood of an assassinated sun deity, in a blend of &quot;Blood of the Bull&quot; and &quot;Blood Gods&quot;.<br /> <br /> - <b><i>Mysterious Places</i></b> i did take <i>the University</i> and <i>Hillcrest Center for Elder Living</i> from, in fact blending them somewhat in the form of a University Hospital/Sanatory (so, not only for the elderly, but people from all ages), that tied in to Ordo Dracul dream vision studies and the Alucinor/Usiri/&quot;Torpor Deep Diving&quot; plotline.<br /> (and the <i>Swamp Indian Hollow</i> too, but that specific part the OD kindred themselves were completely unaware of...)<br /> <br /> - <b><i>Reliquary </i></b>(<b>not </b>Mysterious Places) i filched some stuff from too. The most relevant possibly the <i>Glass Mansion</i>, that in our games became the House that Jack Built, the personal abode/realm of Red Jack, from &quot;The Thing in the Mirror&quot; (also the evolved form of a hollow Mekhet's wandering reflection) filling the role of Blood Mary in our games, Children of Thorns' equivalent cult and all. What also involved a shadow war of sorts with the <i>Baykosh</i> (from Night Horrors: Wicked Dead), as Red Jack spread his influence by replacing (consuming) the reflections of those he made pupils/vassals of through Ars Speculorum gifts, a form of stealth serial diablerie the creature, as a form of reaper, felt duty-bound to track down and deal with (usually by tracking down Jack's kindred anchors).<br /> <br /> So that last one might count as some Danse Macabre use, i guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> PS: corrected the Glass Mansion reference, added what i <b>did</b> get from Mysterious Places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-21-2019, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T11:15:27-07:00","id":1326496,"title":"","content":"I imported and twisted a lot of ideas from dance macabre.Those are the most important:<ul><li>The idea of Kings and Queens of the dammed , vampires so powerful that control multiple domains and princes with the difference that they don\u00b4t have to be from the invictus although the majority are (Ex:Hardesthad or Mitrhas from Masquerade would be kings).</li> <li>The idea of an emperor as a puppet/punishment for camarilla/invictus vampires (Honestly this is hillarious)</li> <li>The holy enginiers (Love them/in my games they are the ones who can do dark miracles instead of the normal lancea who recive other bonuses)</li> <li>The idea of designing plays around tiers , really changed the way I storytelled</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 07-21-2019, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T11:54:55-07:00","id":1326501,"title":"","content":"I've used the tier system extensively, in fact I just started a tier 1 game, and I use the Masquerades and Requiems in place of Second edition Masks and Dirges. I let players make up their own within reason (no one has yet) oh, but you gain willpower from them as if your Mask were a vice and your Dirge was a virtue (using 2e as a guideline). I've been thinking or reintroducing the Discipline skills and Combat auras because the players liked the way they interplayed back in 1e. I'm not sure. Any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T13:26:03-07:00","id":1326788,"title":"","content":"Used a fair bit, off and on.<br /> -Versions of the optional clan boons are standard.<br /> -The Harbingers have been incorporated into a new covenant dealing with death in all its aspects.<br /> -Ported over some of the banes that didn't make it into the newer edition.<br /> -Children of the Stones.<br /> -We used the social maneuvering a little, but it fell out of use.<br /> <br /> Probably some other bits here and there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T18:03:34-07:00","id":1327822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1316770-ever-ran-a-game-using-danse-macabre-content?p=1326496#post1326496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imported and twisted a lot of ideas from dance macabre.Those are the most important:<ul><li>The idea of Kings and Queens of the dammed , vampires so powerful that control multiple domains and princes with the difference that they don\u00b4t have to be from the invictus although the majority are (Ex:Hardesthad or Mitrhas from Masquerade would be kings).</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Hilariously, the one time i did use something like that, it was in a Masquerade chronicle - and more of an emergential self-defense arrangement than conquest proccess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T23:47:50-07:00","id":1340567,"title":"","content":"Oh, how could i forget - there is something from Danse Macabre that i did use (almost) straight in my games.<br /> <br /> The Children of the Thorns - i had forgotten they were from the book due to how i mixed a bunch of stuff from Mary's previous appearance in Mythologies and La Llorona/The White Woman from Shadows of Mexico in my own take of her.<br /> <br /> In my chronicle they were one of many groups involved in a surreal multi-faction shadow war going on for millenia both in the world and in places through mirrors, shadows and dreams and nightmares of both living and dead and had as more notable players:<br /> <br /> - The Sightless Mother and to a major or minor degree, all those who worshipped her, but more importantly those who practiced Cruac (who serve as both worshippers, sources of blood to fuel her own magic <b>and </b>anchors).<br /> <br /> - Bloody Mary (who might also be Pasiphae aka another version of the Sightless Mother) and the Children of the Thorns of course. The Children might also be partly responsible for the spread of Theban Sorcery (an alternative to curtail interest in Cruac - and the Mother's influence) and the tales about VII.<br /> <br /> - La Llorona/The White Woman (who is either an alternate personality of Mary or her Hollow) &amp; her Cihuateteo followers, both witches and kindred, sometimes supporting the Children, sometimes at cross purposes.<br /> <br /> - The Moirai, who might have been founded by the Mother, Pasiphae - or both - but as a group no longer owed true loyalty to either.<br /> <br /> - Red Jack, a latecomer of sorts in the conflict, a Hollow's <i>Ba </i>that once served and betrayed Mary, the White Woman, or possibly both, stealing secrets and followers - her children - in the process. He's more of a war profiteer than actual power in this conflict, though his power grows with every vampire he teaches &quot;Ars Speculorum&quot; (actually a set of Obfuscate devotions) and makes an anchor of in the process.<br /> <br /> - Through a mix of fate, their beliefs, ancient curses, vagaries of their powers or weaknesses and just plain good/bad luck, the ocasional Sethite, Alucinor - or Usiri - will get drafted, pawned or sidelined into the whole surreal mess of a conflict without expecting, wanting or understanding how (the recent return of the Usiri bloodline in contemporary times being just another move in the multi-tiered speed chess puzzle).<br /> <br /> So, i guess i did get some good usage out of the book too after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-06-2022, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-14T00:07:17-08:00","id":1497075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1316770-ever-ran-a-game-using-danse-macabre-content?p=1316857#post1316857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If people are interested, I could do an STV version!<br /> <br /> I'm taking some ideas from <i>The Danse Macabre</i> and some non-vampire crime stuff I've run and developing them a little further, so:<br /> <br /> For a start: Humanity means roughly what it does now, but it merges with Willpower. So Humanity fluctuates, and it's also something you <i>earn</i>, by interacting with your Touchstones and hitting upward breaking points and so on.<br /> <br /> (Being more human isn't saccharine niceness or anything, but if you can crack a smile and save an orphanage, that's usually not going to <i>lose</i> you Humanity.)<br /> <br /> Masquerade and Requiem come back (and I call them Mask and Dirge, for convenience), and act a lot like Origin and Role in <i>Bleeding Edge</i>. The twist is that Mask starts high but is rough to hold onto, while Dirge starts low, but is a cheap buy.<br /> <br /> Disciplines... well, they're getting a look, too, but I need to dice-test my ideas some more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey Rose,<br /> <br /> Did you ever get anywhere with these house rules? I had started thinking Willpower and Humanity should be merged, googled to see if anyone else had done the same, and then found this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}